---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy statement for dingodb.org: no analytics at launch, no non-essential cookies, and accurate description of the deployed configuration."
  path="/privacy/"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  lead="This statement describes the main product website at dingodb.org."
>
  <Callout title="Launch configuration" variant="verified">
    <p>
      The preferred launch configuration is <strong>no analytics</strong> and
      <strong>no non-essential cookies</strong>. This site does not display a
      cookie-consent banner because it does not set non-essential cookies or
      use local storage for tracking.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    Under the current static deployment intent:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>No first-party analytics scripts are shipped with the site build.</li>
    <li>No advertising pixels are loaded.</li>
    <li>No fingerprints or cross-site identity graphs are constructed by site JavaScript.</li>
    <li>
      Optional “copy code” controls use the browser clipboard API locally; they
      do not send code contents to DingoDB servers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting and transport logs</h2>
  <p>
    The operator of whatever host serves these static files (CDN, object
    storage, or reverse proxy) may retain ordinary request logs such as IP
    address, user agent, and URL path for security and reliability. That
    logging is controlled by the host configuration, not by client-side
    tracking on this site. When a production host is designated, operators
    SHOULD document retention there.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Links to <code>docs.dingodb.org</code>, GitHub, and other external sites are
    subject to those sites’ own privacy practices. External links are marked
    and open in a new browsing context where applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>If measurement is added later</h2>
  <p>
    If product measurement becomes required, the project prefers a self-hosted
    or privacy-preserving, cookieless system limited to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>page view</li>
    <li>get-started click</li>
    <li>documentation click</li>
    <li>source/release click</li>
    <li>code-copy success</li>
    <li>survival-demo completion</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Typed search queries, IP-derived profiles, fingerprints, and advertising
    pixels remain out of scope. This page MUST be updated before any such
    system is enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions about this website can be raised through the project’s
    public repository channels:
    <a href="/project/">project page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
